      "title": "Read me",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Video Finish: save, then post-process\n\n1. **Load Video**: pick a video. With generated frames, use **Create Video** here instead.\n2. **Save Video (VideoFinish)** writes the working copy: H.265 CRF 18 and lossless FLAC by default.\n3. **Video Finish: process and save** upscales, resizes and interpolates, and encodes once. It writes `<prefix>_<number>_post.mp4` with the save's number.\n\n**Why the wiring matters**\n- *video → video*: the saver passes its input on unchanged and unencoded. Post-processing then runs after the save and starts from the same frames.\n- *saved → same_number_as*: gives the processed file the save's number.\n\nFrom a video file, post-processing starts from decoded (lossy) frames. When a saved file will be processed later, save it at a lower CRF or 10-bit.\n\n**Models** (not included; see the README for links and licences):\n- `models/upscale_models/`: e.g. Real-CUGAN 4× conservative (`RealCUGAN-4x-conservative.pth`) or `2xLiveActionV1_SPAN_490000.pth`.\n- `models/rife/`: RIFE 4.26 `flownet.pkl`, renamed e.g. `rife4.26.pkl`.\n\nWith *upscale* off, *resize* off and *interpolate* none, nothing is processed and nothing is written."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
